A spoiler follows on accumulating gold.  (It has nothing to do with
leprechans).

Okay, so there I am on level 10 or so, with a pretty good Barbarian going.
I'm not real tough, but I'm getting there.  So I'm minding my own business
when BOOM!  An Op. Throne room.  I spar with a couple of baddies, and then
it's time to pull a King Arthur and head for the hills.

On my flee of terror I pass a friendly Ogre King.  Since I could use some
help and I know the spell of taming, I decide to recruit the bugger.  So
after a long battle, my pet Ogre King name Hobbes and I have finished off
the level and I decide to go picking through the garbage.  To make a long
story short, I'm all of the sudden finding gold everywhere.  Lots of it,
in piles of 400+.  And I'm sure I've already checked everything out.  So
to test my sanity, I double check and room with only 3 piles in it, leave
and come back.  Sure enough, there's gold under them thar piles!  It
didn't take me long to discover that the Ogre King has been picking stuff
up, dropping it, and leaving a pile of gold every time he does so.

To top it off, there was an altar on the next level!  Which leads me to
ask the following question: After getting a better AC through donation,
how come it sometimes gets taken away?  Is it by pissing off my God?  And
if so, how do I avoid this?

This method is much safer than becoming a little "l", and seems to work
better.  I wonder if any other monsters do this?  And does the O. King
have the Midas Touch, or is his supply of gold finite?
